 --- PLAN CONTEXT ---
Plan rationale: The root goal is a single CLI tool with three commands sharing common file/argument validation; I will build the shared foundation (argument parsing, file existence check, CSV reading) first, then implement each command in dependency order so each builds on the previous.
Completed sibling subgoals (already implemented):
  - Implement the CLI entry point and argument parsing: dispatch on the command word, enforce per-command argument counts, and handle the common error cases (unknown command, missing file, wrong arg count) with the specified exit codes and stderr messages
  - Implement a shared CSV reader that reads a file from disk, treats the first line as the header, splits fields on commas, and exposes the header field names and the data rows in file order
  - Implement the `count <file>` command: print the number of data rows (excluding the header) to stdout as a bare integer, exit 0
  - Rewrite src/main/java/com/example/cli/Main.java so that main(String[] args) parses argv and dispatches to check/count/column, enforcing per-command argument counts and the specified exit codes and stderr messages
Do not penalise for absent functionality that will be handled by upcoming sibling subgoals listed above.

 

 

