--- CURRENT SUBGOAL ---
Id: goal-f57c42a4-3871-4454-bfe7-941de202d5b7
Text: Ensure that the `count` command, when invoked with exactly one file argument, does not produce exit code 5 and instead proceeds to count data rows.

--- REMAINING SUBGOALS ---
- goal-05622ad4-1bb7-4f6f-a6f8-f16226a71a04: Audit src/main/java/com/example/cli/Main.java and src/main/java/com/example/cli/reader/CsvReader.java to identify the exact code path that produces exit code 5 when the CLI is invoked with a valid command and file argument, and correct the argument-count validation so that exit 5 is only produced when a known command is given the wrong number of arguments
- goal-f57c42a4-3871-4454-bfe7-941de202d5b7: Ensure that the `count` command, when invoked with exactly one file argument, does not produce exit code 5 and instead proceeds to count data rows.
- goal-77d76793-e597-4e67-968e-1c284adb92b2: Ensure that the `column` command, when invoked with exactly two arguments (file and column name), does not produce exit code 5 and instead proceeds to print column values.
- goal-d3febc51-c77e-403d-a4f8-fa92b5b9de4e: Ensure that the tool produces exit code 1 and prints "no such file: <path>" to stderr when the file argument does not exist, for all three commands.

--- COMPLETED SUBGOALS ---
- goal-91147dea-39e4-42fd-8f79-4c0704cbceb0: Implement the CLI entry point and argument parsing: dispatch on the command word, enforce per-command argument counts, and handle the common error cases (unknown command, missing file, wrong arg count) with the specified exit codes and stderr messages
- goal-f35474b5-5adb-47c7-97b5-030b5031850f: Implement a shared CSV reader that reads a file from disk, treats the first line as the header, splits fields on commas, and exposes the header field names and the data rows in file order
- goal-241e9ac6-5613-420a-89d2-2742748c9103: Implement the `count <file>` command: print the number of data rows (excluding the header) to stdout as a bare integer, exit 0
- goal-0ea62b08-837e-41b7-beb4-f420830571ab: [BUILD_FIX] Make the packaged application start and serve the specified endpoints — the application exits at startup (exit 5) — the process logged nothing diagnostic before the observation ended
- goal-2b9cc4da-d403-4a64-b695-5b924c4c04e1: Implement the `main` method in `src/main/java/com/example/cli/Main.java` to parse `argv`, validate the command word against `check`, `count`, and `column`, and enforce the specific exit codes (1, 2, 3, 4, 5) and stderr messages for invalid inputs, missing files, and unknown commands.
- goal-f45763ac-c8e7-4d5c-a5af-d34b7567129a: Rewrite src/main/java/com/example/cli/Main.java so that main(String[] args) parses argv and dispatches to check/count/column, enforcing per-command argument counts and the specified exit codes and stderr messages
- goal-45748ecc-0ab6-424f-aa60-648bce2dd638: Verify pom.xml configures maven-shade-plugin (or assembly) with Main-Class: com.example.cli.Main in the manifest so the packaged JAR is executable
- goal-759c90ee-6d58-408f-8c62-d3418da960e0: Implement column <file> <name> to print every value of the named column one per line in file order, exiting 0; when the column is absent, print "no such column: <name>" to stderr and exit 4
- goal-de95263e-9cea-4b43-9fbe-0e7537f689a6: Ensure that the `check` command, when invoked with exactly one file argument, does not produce exit code 5 and instead proceeds to read the file and validate rows.

